    "section": "General",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "General:\nUnder this policy, the following general guidelines have been established to ensure comfortable and safe travel in a cost-effective manner:\n• Planning: Travel should be planned well in advance, allowing for better cost optimization and scheduling.\n• Virtual Meetings: Whenever possible, virtual meetings should be organized as an alternative to physical travel.\n• Team Size: The number of individuals travelling in a team should be minimized to reduce expenses.\n• Cost-Effective Locations: Consider choosing the most cost-effective locations for national and global meetings.\n• Expense Minimization: Travel plans should be structured in a way that minimizes overall expenses. For example, if flights are\nprohibitively expensive, consider planning an overnight stay if it results in lower total costs.\n• Cost-Conscious Approach: Employees are expected to adopt an entrepreneurial mind-set, being cost-conscious and conservative\nwhile booking airfare, hotels, and transportation options.\n• Innovative Solutions: Employees are encouraged to find innovative ways to travel in the most cost-effective manner. They are also\nencouraged to provide suggestions to management for adopting such practices to save company costs.\nDomestic Travel Policy\nIt is important to note that this travel policy is designed specifically for business purposes and not for leisure or luxury travel. It is essential\nto prioritize cost reduction and make judicious decisions while utilizing company funds, particularly considering the increased travel costs\npost Covid. The use of technology should be maximized as a means of optimizing travel costs, keeping in mind the advancements in\nartificial intelligence and information technology. However, if travel is unavoidable, employees and associates are expected to exercise a\nprudent approach during their travel endeavour",
