    "section": "1. Air Travel & Hotel Booking",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "1. Air Travel & Hotel Booking:\na. All air travel and hotel accommodation requirements must be booked exclusively through myBiz’s Self Booking Tool (SBT).\nBookings made through any other channels will not be entertained, supported, or reimbursed by Arvind Limited.\nb. Travel Approval (Booking for Self or Interview Candidates, Customers, Vendors, Trainers, Suppliers, etc.):\ni.\nMandatory 7-day advance booking: Tickets must be booked at least 7 days in advance.\nii.\nCheapest corporate fare: Employees are encouraged to select the most cost-effective corporate fare flight available within\nthe preferred travel time.\niii. Approval from reporting manager: All air and hotel bookings require approval from the reporting manager (BM grade).\niv. Booking window through SBT: myBiz will enable the booking option only after receiving approval from the reporting\nmanager.\nc. Overnight Rail Travel: For travel to destinations connected by overnight rail, it is essential to use the train as the mode of\ntransportation.\nd. Monthly MIS: A monthly MIS report will be shared with respective stakeholders to minimize the need for emergency travel.\ne. Overnight Stay for Travel Less than 300 km: If an employee is travelling less than 300 km and requires an overnight stay,\nthe boarding and lodging limits specified in this policy will be applicable.\nf. Separate Flights for Senior Officials: It is advised that senior officials travelling to the same destination on the same day\ntake separate flights.\ng. Reimbursement for Company Guest House Facility: Employees who avail the Company Guest House facility (Annexure\nC), will only be reimbursed for conveyance expenses at actuals according to entitlement.\nDomestic Travel Policy\n2. Women Employees: In addition to the general travel policies, there are specific policies for women employees:\na. Hotel Entitlements: Women employees up to the M3-H1 grades are eligible for hotel limits of the next higher grade if needed.\nThis ensures that women employees have access to suitable and safe accommodation during their travels.\nb. Avoidance of Service Apartments/Guest Houses: Women employees are encouraged to avoid staying in service apartments\nor guest houses. This measure is implemented to prioritize their safety and well-being, as hotels generally offer enhanced\nsecurity and a more controlled environment.\nc. Avoidance of Night Travel: Women employees are advised to avoid night travel whenever possible. This precautionary guideline\nis put in place to ensure their safety and minimize potential risks associated with traveling during late hours.\nBy implementing these women-specific policies, Arvind Limited aims to create a secure and supportive environment for its female\nemployees, promoting their safety and well-being during business travels.\n3. Tour Cancellation, No Show and Delayed Flight:\nThese guidelines aim to provide clarity and accountability in situations related to tour cancellation, no-show, and delayed flights, ensuring\nthat employees are aware of the necessary procedures and their associated responsibilities.\na. Cancellation Process: Employees have the option to cancel their bookings either through the Self Booking Tool (SBT) or by\ncontacting the designated point of contact of myBiz.\nb. Cancellation Policy: It is recommended that travel and stay cancellations are made in accordance with the cancellation policy\nof the respective airlines or hotels. Failure to adhere to the cancellation policy may result in the employee bearing financial\nresponsibility, including non-refundable or cancellation charges imposed by the vendor.\nc. No-Show Charges: In the event of a no-show, where an employee misses the scheduled flight, the charges incurred as a result\nwill be the responsibility of the employee and will be recovered from him/her accordingly.\nd. Delayed Flight: If an employee’s flight is delayed by more than 3 hours from the Estimated Time of Departure (ETD), the\nemployee can cancel or modify the booking through myBiz.",
