    "section": "6. Conveyance",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "6. Conveyance:\na. App-Based Conveyance: Employees are encouraged to utilize app-based conveyance facilities such as Ola, Uber, BluSmart,\nor other cost-effective cab services for point-to-point drops, as well as transfers to airports, railway stations, residences, and\nworkplaces. These services are often more convenient and cost-effective compared to hiring full-day cabs.\nDomestic Travel Policy\nb. Full-Day Cabs: Full-day cab bookings should be made only in scenarios where an employee does not have a return cab/taxi\navailable from the drop location, or when the employee needs to travel to three or more locations on a given day.\nc. Cab Booking Details: Employees should refer to Annexure B for specific details regarding cab bookings. For company-\ncontracted cabs, all bookings should be routed through the business unit admin or travel desk.\nd. Shared Cabs: It is advised that multiple employees traveling to the same destination make arrangements to share cabs. This\npractice promotes cost-efficiency and sustainability.",
