    "section": "9. Settlement of Expenses incurred for Domestic Travel",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "9. Settlement of Expenses incurred for Domestic Travel:\na. Settlement of Expenses: All travel expenses must be claimed through the integrated expense settlement tool available on the\nSelf Booking Tool (SBT) on One Arvind.\nb. Timely Settlement: Employees are requested to complete the travel settlement process for self-spent amounts within 15 days\nof the trip. Failure to settle within this timeframe will result in auto-settlement on the 16th day, and no reimbursement will be\nprovided under such circumstances.\nc. Settlement Process: The settlement process can only be initiated once the employee has returned from the official tour. This\nsettlement should be done through the web-based in-house expense management tool available on One Arvind.\nd. Original Bills/Invoices: All expenses incurred by official travellers must be supported by original bills/invoices, such as cab\nbills, food bills, and other applicable receipts as per the policy. The bills/invoices should clearly mention the details of the\nexpenses, including the date, location, and services availed. Bills/invoices without these details will not be considered valid for\nreimbursement.\ne. Guest Entertainment Expenses: Expenditures related to entertaining guests should be claimed separately as business\nexpenditures, subject to necessary approval.\nDomestic Travel Policy\nf. Special Sanction: Any expenses that exceed the defined entitlements will require special sanction from the Head of the\nDepartment who holds a position at the BM-H3 level or above.\ng. Non-Reimbursable Items: The list of Non-Reimbursable items is provided in Annexure B.",
