    "section": "10. Attendance and Leave",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "10. Attendance and Leave:\nThese guidelines ensure that employees comply with attendance procedures during official travel and adhere to the necessary protocols\nfor requesting and availing leave. This promotes transparency and accountability in managing attendance and leave during official trips.\na. Regularizing Attendance: Employees are required to regularize their attendance by applying for “Outdoor Travel” in the\nDarwinbox system, following the guidelines outlined in the Attendance Policy. This ensures proper tracking and documentation\nof their presence during official trips.\nb. Leave during Official Trip: In the event that an employee avails leave during an official trip, they will not be eligible for any\nallowance or reimbursement for the period or day of leave. The employee must apply for leave according to the company’s\nleave policy in such circumstances.\nEnclosures\n1. Annexure A - Mode of Travel, Lodging & Boarding entitlement and Classification of Cities\n2. Annexure B - Cab Booking Matrix & Non-Reimbursable Items\n3. Annexure C - Guest house Details\n4. Annexure D - Statewise GST Detials\n5. Annexure E - MMT Transition Phases\nDomestic Travel Policy",
