    "text": "GENERAL TRAVEL GUIDELINES:\nEmployees must adopt an entrepreneurial mind-set, planning well in advance, utilizing virtual meetings when feasible, and minimizing team sizes. Travel is for business purposes only, not luxury. Use technology and AI options to optimize expenses.\nAUTHORISATION RULES:\nAll self-bookings or guest-bookings must be approved by the reporting manager who holds a position at the BM grade. If the immediate manager is below BM grade, the tool automatically escalates the workflow to the skip-level manager who is at the BM grade or above.\nAIR & HOTEL PROCEDURES:\nAll flights and hotel requirements must be booked exclusively through MMT's myBiz Self Booking Tool (SBT). Off-channel bookings are non-reimbursable. Tickets require a mandatory 7-day advance booking window and selection of the cheapest corporate fare available. The SBT booking option will unlock only after manager approval. Train must be used for destinations connected by overnight rail. Senior officials travelling to the same destination should take separate flights.",
