    "text": "EXPENSE CLAIM WORKFLOW:\nClaims for self-spent amounts must be initiated through the One Arvind online dashboard tool within a strict 15-day window from the trip's end. On the 16th day, system auto-settlement locks the entry, and no reimbursement is paid. All filings require crisp invoices showing the dates, location, and services availed. Guest entertainment must be filed separately as a business expense. Exceeding tier allowance caps requires a special systemic sanction from a Head of Department at the BM-H3 grade level or above.\nATTENDANCE DARWINBOX RULES:\nEmployees are required to regularize their travel dates by applying for 'Outdoor Travel' within the Darwinbox HRMS module. Taking personal leave during an official company trip cancels out all allowance eligibility and expense reimbursements for those specific calendar dates.\nAnnexure Index: Annexure A (Entitlements & City Classification), Annexure B (Cab Matrix & Non-Reimbursable items), Annexure C (Guest house details), Annexure D (Statewise GST details), Annexure E (MMT transition chart). Management holds rights to change this framework without prior notice.",
