    "section": "OBJECTIVE & PACKERS VISITS",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "JOINING & RELOCATION POLICY:\nObjective: Regulate the norms around the joining process of all new recruits and to mitigate the hardship due to relocation from one city to another.\nApplicability: Applicable to all Management / staff cadre employees who are part of Arvind Limited and/or its subsidiaries.\nEffective Date: 21.09.2023\nVISIT OPTIONS ON JOINING:\na. Pre-Joining Visit: New recruit and spouse are eligible for a pre-joining property/school lookup visit for a maximum period of 3 days. Reimbursed for to-and-fro travel expenses for self and spouse (children included only for school admission layouts).\nb. Post-Joining Visit / Leave: If the pre-joining option was not used, the employee is eligible for 3 days of paid leave to visit their legacy location to manage relocation tasks. Reimbursed for a one-time family transit layout matching the Travel Policy.\nHOUSEHOLD GOODS TRANSPORTATION:\nPayment is managed against actual costs. Payout covers packing, unpacking, loading, unloading, service tax, and insurance options.\n• Logic Constraint 1: If distance between current location and posting is < 700 kms, maximum cap is Rs. 50 per km or actuals (whichever value is lesser). Income tax is grossed up for the employee based on their tax bracket.\n• Logic Constraint 2: If distance is > 700 kms, maximum cap scales to Rs. 60 per km or actuals (whichever value is lesser). Income tax is grossed up based on their tax bracket.",
