    "section": "VEHICLE TRANSIT, STAYS & RECOVERY CLAUSE",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "VEHICLE TRANSPORTATION RULES:\nOnly one personal car is covered. If moved via Packers & Movers, reimbursement is calculated at a fixed Rs. 10.0 per km based on map distance. If driven by self or an assigned driver, reimbursement covers mileage at Rs. 10.0 per km + toll charges on actuals + driver wages. Driver wages are capped at Rs. 600 for an 8-hour trip, and Rs. 50 per hour after 8 hours. Travel food is capped at a maximum of Rs. 200 per meal threshold.\nBROKERAGE & HOUSE DEPOSITS:\nBrokerage: Up to 1 month's rent is reimbursable against a valid receipt if the individual opts for HRA. This benefit can be claimed only once during their entire tenure and must be utilized within a maximum window of 1 year from the employee's date of joining.\nHouse Deposit Advance: Provided to the recruit as an advance, interest-free, and recovered from payroll across 10 equal monthly instalments.\nREIMBURSEMENTS & CRITICAL CLAWBACK CLAUSE:\nNotice Pay Buyouts / Variable Pay / Joining Bonuses are subject to management approvals and release only after submitting the official Full & Final settlement document from the previous employer. Any amount exceeding standard limits requires special sanction from the CEO (for business teams) or Corporate HR Head (for corporate lines). Invoices must bear the recruit's legal name and be claimed within 1 year from the date of joining.\n• THE 1-YEAR RECOVERY RULE: If an employee resigns or terminates their employment within 1 year of joining, the complete sum (Joining Bonus + Relocation Expense + Notice Pay Buyout + Variable Pay Reimbursements + Brokerage) will be recovered in full from their final F&F payroll settlement. Tax laws apply based on active legal brackets.",
