    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "b. Terms:\ni.\nIn the event of an employee using his personal vehicle, the amount reimbursed will be\non the kms. Travelled for four wheeler @ Rs. 10.00 / - per km and for two wheeler @\nRs. 5.00 per km.\nii.\nEmployees can make the necessary claim in the system – Orapps – ESMS – Entry –\nConveyance Expense. The employee will have to input the total kms travelled in the\nday and also the to and fro kms from residence to official location of posting which\nshall get deducted. Detailed explanation on the authorized claim is given in point no ix.\niii.\nFor an employee using taxi for conveyance, the reimbursement will be done on actuals\nas declared by him/ her in the system. Appropriate bills / vouchers would have to be\nsubmitted along with the claim.\niv.\nThese limits shall be applicable across India.\nv.\nIf more than one person have travelled in the same vehicle, then the individual who\nhas actually incurred the cost shall only claim the reimbursement.\nvi.\nThe local conveyance expense shall be approved only by BM grade employees of\nrespective departments. It is the manager’s responsibility to ensure the authenticity of\nclaims made.\nHR Policy\nClassification:\nInternal\nIssue Date:\n30.06.2022\nEffective From:\n01.07.2022\nPolicy Number:\nARV|COR",
