    "text": "ARV|ELC_SHA|008|010422\nPolicy incorporates the legislation titled The Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention,\nProhibition and Redressal) Act, (defined as “Act”) and its Rules (defined as “Rules”) notified and\npublished on 9th December 2013.\nArvind and familiar with the issues relating to sexual harassment, as may be nominated by\nManagement.\nArvind reserves the right to remove Presiding Officer and/or any Member of the AIC, before the period\nof three years, by assigning reasons in writing without any further process or inquiry where the\nPresiding Officer or any member of AIC.\nProbable reasons for removal include:\ni.\ncontravenes the provisions of Section 16 of the Act; or\nii.\nHas been convicted for an offence or an inquiry into an offence under any law for the time being\nin force is pending against him; or\niii.\nHas been found guilty in any disciplinary proceedings or a disciplinary proceeding is pending\nagainst a member; or has so abused his position as to render his continuance in office prejudicial\nto the public interest.\nGuidelines for the Management:\ni.\nVacancy created due to such removal shall be filled by fresh nomination in accordance with the\nprovisions of the Act.\nii.\nManagement shall fill up the vacancy in the AIC as may be created by removal, death, expiration\nof appointment term, resignation by Member etc. within 15 days from such event.\niii.\nManagement shall provide office space/premises to AIC to carry out functions and working of\nthe AIC.\niv.\nPresiding Officer shall appoint a \"Contact Officer\" amongst the member of AIC, who will be\navailable at designate place and time for the purpose of administering this policy.\nv.\nExternal Member shall be paid minimum remuneration Rs. 250 per day and conveyance\nallowances as per Arvind’s policy. AIC members who are employees of Arvind shall not be\npaid additional remuneration except as per their salary structure.\nvi.\nWhere AIC is composed of members in addition to the minimum prescribed quorum, in the event\nof an inquiry, the Presiding Officer shall prefer representation from AIC member of that\nadministrative unit where the complaint is lodged.\nvii.\nIn each inquiry, the minimum quorum shall consist of 50% women representation in AIC. In\nconducting the inquiry, a minimum of 3 members of the AIC including the Presiding Officershall\nbe present.\nviii.\nAIC will be treated as an independent committee and not as part of the Arvind Management. For\nthe purposes of smoother administration, the AIC will route the communications to management\nthrough the Presiding Officer.\nix.\nAIC is vested with the same powers as that of a civil court under the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908\nfor the purpose of making inquiry, summoning and enforcing attendance and production of\nrequired documents.\nx.\nNo person, against whom a complaint is made, shall be a part of AIC. In case the Aggrieved\nWoman’s complaint is against a member of AIC, such member will not participate in any stage\nof review or inquiry into such complaint.\nPrivate & Confidential\nOnly for Internal Circulation\nPage 5\nHR Policy\nClassification:\nInternal\nIssue Date:\n31.03.2022\nEffective From:\n01.05.2025\nPolicy Number:",
