    "section": "TERM AND TENURE OF AIC MEMBERS",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "TERM AND TENURE OF AIC MEMBERS:\nEvery member of the AIC (except for External Member) shall hold office for a period of three years or\ncompletion of the age of 58 years, whichever is earlier, from the date of nomination by Management.\nPost completion of initial period of three years, members may be re-nominated/re-elected for one\nadditional term. Any member who has been removed under Clause VIII shall not be eligible for re -\nnomination/re-election.",
