    "section": "REDRESSAL PROCEDURE",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "REDRESSAL PROCEDURE:\n1.\nComplaint Lodging:\nThis policy is gender neutral and covers with equal rigour all genders, i.e. men, women and\ntransgender. This policy also prohibits same-sex harassment.\nWho can file a complaint?\nAs provided in the Act and the rules, the following can file a complaint:\ni.\nAggrieved woman\nii.\nCT: Where the Aggrieved Woman is unable to make a complaint on account of her\nmental/physical incapacity, a complaint may be filed by:\na.\nHer relative or friend; or\nb.\nHer co-worker; or\nc.\nAny person who has knowledge of the incident with the written consent of the\nAggrieved Woman, or\nd.\nA special educator (in case of mental incapacity), or\ne.\nThe guardian or authority under whose care she is receiving treatment (in case of\nmental incapacity)\nf.\nWhere the Aggrieved Woman is dead, a complaint may be filed by any person who\nhas knowledge of the incident/s with the written consent of her legal heir/s.\nAny CT (including an Aggrieved Woman) may lodge a written complaint or via e-mail by using any\none of the following mechanisms:\ni.\nThe Supervisor / Reporting Manager / any other trusted person in the line of hierarchy, or\nii.\nThe Respective Business Unit HR Head, or\niii.\nThe whistleblowing channels including:\na.\nHotline: 18002008301\nb.\nEmail: arvind@ethicshelpline.in\nc.\nPortal /Website: www.in.kpmg.com/ethicshelpline/arvind/\nPrivate & Confidential\nOnly for Internal Circulation\nPage 6\nHR Policy\nClassification:\nInternal\nIssue Date:\n31.03.2022\nEffective From:\n01.05.2025\nPolicy Number:",
