    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "ARV|ELC_SHA|008|010422\nPolicy incorporates the legislation titled The Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention,\nProhibition and Redressal) Act, (defined as “Act”) and its Rules (defined as “Rules”) notified and\npublished on 9th December 2013.\ng.\nOn the completion of its inquiry, the AIC shall provide a report of its findings to the\nemployer, within a period of 10 (ten) days from the date of completion of the inquiry and\nsuch report must be made available to the concerned parties.\nh.\nManagement has 60 (sixty) days to execute the AIC recommendation.\nvii.\nInterim Action\nDuring the pendency of the inquiry, and on a request made by the Aggrieved Woman, the\nAIC may take any of the following interim actions:\na.\nTo offer medical help and counselling to the Aggrieved Woman, if required.\nb.\nTo transfer the Aggrieved Woman and/or the RE to an alternate work location (work\nfrom home, another office, another floor etc.).\nc.\nTo grant leave to the Aggrieved Woman up to a period of 3 (three) months, which\nwould be in addition to the entitled leaves of such Aggrieved Woman.\nd.\nTo suspend the RE for defined period or until the inquiry proceedings are completed\ne.\nTo ensure that the reporting relationship is suspended\nf.\nTo ensure that the Aggrieved Woman is not subject to appraisal by the RE\ng.\nIn case, RE is an outsider, ensure that the RE shall not be allowed to enter Arvind\npremises except for the purpose of attending the proceedings.\nFor complaints raised by CT (who is not an aggrieved woman)\nThe CT must complain in writing. The CT must provide all relevant information to facilitate an inquiry.\nDetails of complaints will be kept confidential and HR will conduct inquiries with regard to complaints\nmade. Such an enquiry will not be conducted by AIC. All the parties involved will be given an opportunity\nof being heard.\nIf, on inquiry, the complaint is found to be genuine, action will be taken against the RE. In such a\ncase, HR can recommend action for sexual harassment as misconduct in accordance with the Other\nPolicies as applicable to the RE. If HR arrives at the conclusion that the allegation has not been proved,\nit may recommend that no action has to be taken against the RE.",
