    "section": "DISCIPLINARY ACTION",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "DISCIPLINARY ACTION\nOn conclusion of the inquiry, if the allegation/s against the RE is/are proved, appropriate action against the\nguilty may be recommended. Such a recommendation must be in line with the Act or the Other Policies and\nmay include:\na.\nWritten warning\nb.\nWritten apology\nc.\nReprimand/Censure\nd.\nWithholding of promotion\ne.\nWithholding of pay rise or increments\nf.\nTerminating the RE from service\ng.\nUndergoing a counselling session\nh.\nCarrying out community service\ni.\nMonetary compensation\nj.\nCommunity service\nGUIDELINE TO BE KEPT IN MIND BY AIC WHILE RECOMMENDING ACTION\n1.\nTo conduct the inquiry as per the principles of natural justice and in a confidential manner.\n2.\nAIC members to be intimated of meetings and agenda in writing and/or electronic communication\nby the Presiding Officer. Minutes of all meetings to be recorded, confirmed, and adopted.\n3.\nIn cases where the AIC has recommended to Management for compensation to be made to theCT,\nthen the said amount shall be deducted from the salary of the RE and paid to the CT or her legal\nheir/s.\n4.\nIn case of complaint by an Aggrieved Woman, if the RE fails to pay the sum referred as above, the\nAIC may forward the order for recovery of the sum as an arrear of land revenue to the concerned District\nOfficer.\n5.\nWhere the AIC arrives at a conclusion that the allegation against the RE is malicious, the AIC may\nrecommend to the Management to start an inquiry on the suspected malicious complaint.\n6.\nWhere the AIC arrives at a conclusion that during the enquiry any witness has given false evidence\nor produced any forged or misleading document, it shall recommend to the Management to take\nappropriate action.",
