    "section": "PROTECTION AGAINST RETALIATION",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "PROTECTION AGAINST RETALIATION:\nRegardless of the outcome of the complaint made in good faith, the CT, or any person providing information,\nor any witness, shall be protected from any form of retaliation. No unfair treatment will be meted out to the\nCT lodging the complaint in good faith. While dealing with complaints of sexual harassment, the AIC shall\nensure that the CT or the witness are not victimized or discriminated against by the RE. Any form of retaliation\nwould be dealt as per the Act or the Other Policies, as may apply. Examples of retaliation may include, but are\nnot limited to, unsubstantiated negative performance evaluation, continued harassment in any form,\ndiscriminatory treatment, failure to provide or consider the CT or any witness for a deserved role, title, training,\nor promotion.",
