    "section": "MALICIOUS COMPLAINT",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "MALICIOUS COMPLAINT:\nIn case the HR/AIC, on conclusion of the inquiry finds that the allegation was malicious or that the CT has made\nthe complaints knowing it to be false, or has produced any forged / misleading document, it will recommend\naction to be taken under the Act or the Other Policies, as may apply, after conducting a separate inquiry\nagainst the CT who has made the complaint. In all such cases the malicious intent on the part of the CT must\nbe established. Mere inability to substantiate a complaint or provide adequate proof will not attract action\nagainst the CT.\nPrivate & Confidential\nOnly for Internal Circulation\nPage 10\nHR Policy\nClassification:\nInternal\nIssue Date:\n31.03.2022\nEffective From:\n01.07.2023\nPolicy Number:",
