    "section": "SEXUAL HARASSMENT LEGAL DEFINITION",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "LEGAL DEFINITION OF SEXUAL HARASSMENT:\nIncludes unwelcome, sexually determined behaviors (direct or by implication):\n1. Physical contact and sexual advances.\n2. Demand or request for sexual favors.\n3. Sexually colored remarks or jokes.\n4. Showing pornography or offensive visual materials via screensavers/emails.\n5. Unwelcome physical, verbal, non-verbal, or written conduct of a sexual nature.\nQUID PRO QUO & HOSTILE WORK ENVIRONMENT CONDITIONS:\nHarassment is established if the following conditions link to an unwelcome sexual behavior:\ni. Implicit or explicit promises of preferential treatment in employment.\nii. Implicit or explicit threats of detrimental treatment or future career blockages.\niii. Hostile Environment: Interference with work or creating an intimidating, offensive, or humiliating ecosystem.\niv. Humiliating treatment that directly risks or impacts personal health or workplace safety.\nv. Supervisor Pressure: Requesting sexual favors in exchange for promised increments, higher ratings, title promotions, or using non-cooperation as a ground to execute payroll termination or negative appraisals. Gossip regarding an individual's private sex life or body comments are subject to disciplinary actions under abetment rules.",
