    "section": "INQUIRY LIFECYCLE & SLA TARGETS",
    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "THE STATUTORY INQUIRY TIMELINE MATRIX:\n• Filing Window: Complaints must be submitted within 3 months of the incident date (or 3 months from the final date in a connected series of events). The AIC can grant an extension of an additional 3 months if justifiable preventative bottlenecks are recorded in writing.\n• Legal Representation: Legal practitioners are banned from representing either party before the AIC at any stage.\n• Conciliation Path: The AIC can enable informal conciliation paths (warnings, counseling, or orientations) at the victim's request, but cannot force direct resolution or settlement between parties.\n• Inquiry Steps & Processing SLAs:\n - Step A (6 Copies): Complainant submits 6 hard copies of text statements along with witness indexes.\n - Step B (7 Days): AIC runs a preliminary check and forwards 1 copy to the Respondent within 7 calendar days.\n - Step C (10 Days): The Respondent must submit their formal defensive statement within 10 working days.\n - Step D (90 Days): The AIC has a strict limit of 90 days to finalize the complete evidentiary inquiry.\n - Step E (15 Days Notice): AIC can terminate proceedings if either party skips 3 consecutive sessions without cause, giving a mandatory 15-day warning layout.\n - Step F (10 Days Report): Finding reports must land with the Employer within 10 days of inquiry completion.\n - Step G (60 Days Execution): Management has a hard limit of 60 days to enforce the final AIC remediation order.",
