    "chunkType": "rule",
    "text": "DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS ENFORCEMENT CHOICES:\nIf allegations are proved, the AIC can recommend the following penalties based on severity:\na. Written warning or explicit written apology.\nb. Formal Reprimand or Censure.\nc. Withholding of salary rises, promotion blocks, or merit increments.\nd. Monetary compensation deducted directly from the payroll of the guilty individual.\ne. Mandating continuous community service layout or behavioral counseling sessions.\nf. Full termination from services with a permanent blacklist tag.\nPAYROLL SALARY DESTRUCTION COMPENSATION:\nApproved victim compensation amounts are deducted straight from the Respondent's payroll check. If the individual has resigned or fails to settle the amount, the AIC will forward the order to the active District Officer to recover the financial sum as an arrear of land revenue.\nMALICIOUS ENTRY PROTECTION:\nIf an inquiry proves that a complaint was intentionally malicious, false, or supported by forged documents, the AIC will trigger a separate disciplinary inquiry against the Complainant. Clear malicious intent must be established; an inability to provide enough proof does not count as a false complaint. Witness fraud follows the same penalty path.",
